WEBVTT

NOTE Visual text from a silent video.

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.400
Processing on a sensing satellite is not the same as operating an orbital cloud.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.100
Data origins, scale and expected service are different.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:22.000
Identify each proposal’s use case before comparing them.

4
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:29.400
A full image may contain information irrelevant to a specific detection task.

5
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:36.100
This example keeps selected regions and transmits a smaller result.

6
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:44.000
Validate that selection: discarding information can also lose events.

7
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.400
A prototype tests a particular combination of power, duration and environment.

8
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:58.100
A service also needs availability, maintenance and sustained capacity.

9
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:06.000
The untested region remains a hypothesis even when the pilot works.

10
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:13.400
Separated copies reduce some risks shared by a ground location.

11
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:20.100
Restoring data also needs links, keys and a working system.

12
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:28.000
Test the complete recovery, not merely the existence of the archive.

13
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:35.400
A remote update can change instructions and configuration.

14
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:42.100
It does not add physical memory or automatically replace a damaged component.

15
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:50.000
Design autonomy, redundancy and end of mission from the start.

16
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:57.400
The analysis does not end when hardware deploys and starts processing.

17
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:04.100
Include link coordination, failure handling and retirement at end of life.

18
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:12.000
The proposal must explain who operates it, who is accountable and how it ends.

